# Plugin sync writes canonical scripts here — not source, not committed.
.claude/scripts/
.claude/contracts/
.baseline-*.sh
__pycache__/
.claude/anatomy.md
.claude/worktrees/
docs/leadv2/.pulse-*
docs/leadv2/.broad-status-prev.json
.repowise/
docs/leadv2/glm-deferred.jsonl
docs/leadv2/glm-deferred.d/
# FP-06 fix-round (H4): runtime telemetry appended once per dispatch terminal —
# a generated artifact, not an authored doc; capped in dispatch-code, ignored here.
# .lock* also covers the mkdir-fallback lock dir (*.lock.d, flock-less hosts).
docs/leadv2/model-select-telemetry.csv
docs/leadv2/model-select-telemetry.csv.lock*
docs/leadv2/.arm-exceptions-*
docs/leadv2/.codex-credits-empty.stamp
docs/leadv2/*.lock
# PROJECT_ROOT-leak residue from an unisolated dispatch run under tests/ (L5 fix,
# V3-GLM-LADDER-01 R3) -- must never be tracked, or the leak becomes invisible.
plugins/leadv2/scripts/tests/docs/
# Control-plane state must never be committed below the plugin's scripts cwd.
/plugins/leadv2/scripts/docs/
plugins/leadv2/scripts/tests/.claude/

# HANDOFF-AND-STATE-NOISE-01 (2026-08-21): mirror persona-engine's convention.
# Lane handoff artifacts and generated orchestration state are per-run outputs —
# architect prepasses, review diffs, stream jsonl, costs, session maps, review-<hash>
# stamps. 268 of them were showing as uncommitted changes here while the identical
# files are ignored in persona-engine, which is why this repo looked permanently
# dirty. Authored docs at the top of docs/handoff/ and docs/leadv2/ stay tracked.
#
# HANDOFF-ARTIFACTS-GITIGNORED-01 (2026-08-31): the blanket rule above ignored
# proof, not just churn — a lane's roundN-red/ output (the only durable
# evidence a negative control ever went red) and its report.md/brief.md never
# reached git, and because the path was ignored, DELETING one was invisible
# in `git status` too (a lane could destroy another lane's evidence silently).
# Allowlist the artifacts that are actual evidence; everything else under
# docs/handoff/<id>/ (stream jsonl, session maps, locks, regenerated diffs,
# stamps — per-run scratch) stays default-ignored.
#
# D2-UNBLIND-AND-THIRD-STATE-M0M1-01 (M0): the worker's own deliverable report
# (*.full.md / *.summary.md) is evidence a round finished, not per-run scratch.
# 184 of 281 on-disk reports were invisible to git (ignored at random — the 97
# tracked ones merely predate the blanket rule), so a worker that finished
# without committing read as "produced nothing" and was re-dispatched, each
# dispatch erasing the previous round's report.
!docs/handoff/*/*.full.md
!docs/handoff/*/*.summary.md
!docs/handoff/*/persona-engine-close-commands.txt
#
# HANDOFF-ARTIFACTS-ALLOWLIST-IS-NAME-BASED-01 (round 2, 2026-09-04): the line
# above (and the report.md/brief*.md/fix-round*.md/continue-round*.md/
# architect-prepass.md/divergence.md lines that used to sit further down) each
# enumerated one NAME. report-e4-round.md, fix-round-1.md and mission-close.md
# are all lane documents that finished a round, exactly like report.md or
# *.full.md, but none of them matched any enumerated name, so a brand-new kind
# of document was invisible by default the day it was first written. A lane's
# own documents are markdown; visibility keys on that extension, not on an
# ever-growing name list, so ANY *.md written directly under docs/handoff/<id>/
# is a document and stays visible. This does NOT widen to "everything in the
# directory": non-.md siblings (context.yaml, .gate1-passed, round*-red/) are
# not documents and keep their own, separately-motivated exceptions below —
# a stray context.yaml-adjacent tarball, editor backup or scratch.txt must
# still default-ignore (test-handoff-artifacts-tracked.sh RED control (b)
# proves widening to `!docs/handoff/*/*` breaks exactly this mirror).
docs/handoff/*/*
!docs/handoff/*/*.md
!docs/handoff/*/round*-red
docs/leadv2/review-*
docs/leadv2/status-snapshot.json
docs/leadv2/founder-status*.md
docs/leadv2/glm-deferred*
docs/leadv2/.arm-exceptions-*
docs/leadv2/.pulse-beat-last
docs/leadv2/.board-empty-since
docs/leadv2/.founder-status-epoch
docs/leadv2/.codex-credits-empty.stamp
# LANE-STATE-LEAK-01: RENDER-class collisions delete the local copy outright
# (no backup); this pattern only guards new STANDARD-class backups going
# forward. The two pre-existing ones (active.yaml, open-threads.md) are
# already tracked and are deliberately left alone.
docs/leadv2/*.pre-controlplane-backup
# Per-dispatch task journals. 291 are already tracked from before this rule and are
# left alone deliberately — untracking them is a separate, reviewable call. New ones
# stop dirtying the repo on every dispatch.
docs/leadv2/tasks/*/
docs/leadv2/bus.jsonl
docs/leadv2/merge-queue.jsonl
docs/leadv2/questions/
# Burn-governor runtime ledger — not source.
docs/leadv2/burn-deferred.jsonl
docs/leadv2/burn-deferred.d/

# Local session config and a stray review artifact at the handoff root.
.claude/cache/
docs/handoff/dispatch-*-review-*.md
# fix-round*.md, continue-round*.md, architect-prepass.md and divergence.md
# used to each need their own !-line here; all four are *.md and now covered
# by `!docs/handoff/*/*.md` above (HANDOFF-ARTIFACTS-ALLOWLIST-IS-NAME-BASED-01).
# context.yaml and .gate1-passed are NOT documents (structured lead state /
# gate marker, never authored prose) and are deliberately NOT part of that
# extension rule; they keep their own exception because the 2026-08-31 fix
# (commit 6f6b55b, "the phase gate demanded artifacts .gitignore forbade
# committing") needs them trackable regardless of the document-visibility
# rule above — do not fold them into a "non-.md siblings stay ignored" mirror
# assertion, that would require deleting this line and reintroduce that gate
# failure.
!docs/handoff/*/context.yaml
!docs/handoff/*/.gate1-passed
!docs/handoff/*/divergence.md

# REGISTRY-MUST-LEAVE-GIT-01: docs/leadv2/active.yaml is LIVE cross-worktree
# registry state (see plugins/leadv2/scripts/leadv2-state-path.sh /
# LEAD-CONTROL-PLANE-01). Tracking it in git meant every worktree checkout
# got its own frozen copy at the branch's commit -- fourteen divergent
# copies measured 2026-09-04. The resolver already redirects live reads/
# writes to ~/.claude/leadv2-state/<repo-slug>/active.yaml and symlinks
# docs/leadv2/active.yaml -> there; git must never re-materialize a real
# file at this path (git checkout only recreates a path git remembers as
# tracked -- untracking it stops the next worktree from getting a frozen copy).
/docs/leadv2/active.yaml
